       <narrative xml:lang="EN">A total of 52 MPs of 7 PACs of seven PAs discussed major highlights and observations of the 59th report of the Auditor General and discussed the process of follow-up to settle arrears.
LJHRC reviewed 2 bills:  Bills to amend some Acts on Sexual Violence 2022 and Bills to amend some Acts on Criminal Offences and Criminal Procedures with PSPs support
5 bills reviewed and consulted (Technical Education and Vocational Training Council Bill; Madarsa Education Board Bill Girl child protection bill; Amendment bill for the election conduction, management, and integration of related laws; Bill on coordination between the province and local levels and dispute management
8 oversights were completed (Oversight of Flood Affected areas and status of services; oversight of road construction, river embankments; oversight of forest encroachment; budget and policy oversights, legislative oversights etc)
PSP supported the Law, Justice and Human Rights Committee for 7 oversight missions to review the status of jails in 8 districts of 3 PAs. 
The legislative assessment of 20 Acts of 4 PAs (PA 1, Madhesh, Bagmati, Lumbini) completed, which provided information on the quality of laws formulated in 4 PAs. The assessment has covered Acts in the areas of GESI, human rights, Climate change, environment and anti-corruption and good governance
The Law, Justice and Human Rights Committee of FP discussed on research report and provided recommendations to the Ministry. The Legislative Management Committee of the National Assembly finalized the PLS report of the &#x201c;Public Procurement Act, 2063 committee and issued 38-point recommendations to the government.
8 policy dialogues on budget allocation and spending on SDGs agendas on climate action&#x201d; ,&#x201c;gender equality , natural disaster and Nepal government&#x2019;s DRR/M plan and strategies , disaster preparedness , good governance and SDG, etc. is completed.
1 meet on inter-legislative interaction between Speakers and Deputy Speakers concluded with a follow-up of previous meets&#x2019; towards strengthening the cooperation and coordination among legislative bodies and help ensuring consistency in parliamentary practice.
Over 160 staff(23% women) participated in a series of 28 capacity-building events on verbatim management, GESI, Parliamentary Report Writing, Photography-Videography, Website Management, Library Management etc.
8 interactions completed ( 4 Interactions between experienced women leaders of the FP and the women MPs and potential women leaders of and 4 events on Dialogues on Increasing the Candidacy of Women and Marginalized Groups in the Upcoming Election)
Over 140 journalists oriented through series of training including  budget reporting , climate reporting , disaster affairs reporting , and Experience and Challenges of Parliamentary Journalism in PAs , and &#x201c;Parliamentary Reporting beyond National Frontiers: experiences from India and Nepal&#x201d; etc. Besides this, the Journalists Society for Parliamentary Affairs of Lumbini Province coordinated and documented the best parliamentary practices of all 7 PAs.
20 episodes of a radio program via 150 plus radios aired on different thematic issues such as good governance in PAs, the status of bills in parliaments, gender equality, elections, youths, climate change, human rights, parliament affairs etc. and reached out to over 500000 audiences via social media platforms
8 events/programs organized.
3 PAs marked international womens day and conducted 3 interactions on the Issues and challenges of the women migrant workers. 5 radio programs with a focus on discourse on Dignified Menstruation  aired between 25 Nov-10 Dec to mark 16 days of activism against Gender-based Violence
6 events on MPs interaction with Youth/ PA day, Open Parliament Week and youth participation, theatre program three transit, radio program on youth participation in parliament, youth and electoral democracy, etc organized that reached out to over 1 million audiences through social platforms.
